# Local .terraform directories
**/.terraform/*
terraform/old

*.nf
# .tfstate files
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Crash log files
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Exclude all .tfvars files, which are likely to contain sensitive data, such as
# password, private keys, and other secrets. These should not be part of version
# control as they are data points which are potentially sensitive and subject
# to change depending on the environment.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json

# The operator's answers document (docs/globus-setup.md step 3.1). It holds no
# secret — the client secret is a reference the schema enforces — but it is one
# deployment's identifiers, and D15 keeps those out of the code.
globus-answers.yaml
globus-answers.*.yaml

# The setup wizard's answers document (docs/deployer-first-hour.md). Same reason:
# no secret — the wizard refuses a credential field outright — but it holds one
# deployment's domain, issuer, Cloudflare account and bucket. The deployer guide
# says to version it, and that means in the deployer's OWN deployment repository,
# beside their Terraform root, never in this one. Ignored here because this
# repository's root files are only report-only to the publish gate, so a
# committed copy would not be blocked. `.json` too: `cloudpipe setup` writes JSON
# when the --answers path ends in it.
cloudpipe-answers.yaml
cloudpipe-answers.yml
cloudpipe-answers.*.yaml
cloudpipe-answers.json

# terraform/.terraform.lock.hcl IS committed, deliberately — it used to be
# ignored here ("don't need terraform locks"), which meant every `terraform
# init` re-resolved providers against the registry and re-fetched SHA256SUMS to
# establish trust. That is a live network dependency on each provider's release
# hosting, and it broke CI on 2026-08-12 when the checksum fetch for
# gavinbunney/kubectl (hosted on GitHub Releases, not the HashiCorp CDN) timed
# out. With the lock committed, init verifies against recorded hashes instead.
#
# Consequence: provider upgrades are now explicit. `terraform init` will no
# longer drift you onto a newer patch release; run
#   terraform init -upgrade && terraform providers lock -platform=...
# and commit the result. See .github/workflows/ci.yaml (terraform_lint).

# Ignore override files as they are usually used to override resources locally and so
# are not checked in
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Include override files you do wish to add to version control using negated pattern
# !example_override.tf

# Saved plan files from `terraform plan -out=...`. The upstream template leaves
# this commented out as an example; it is enabled here because three of them
# (1.2-1.3 MB each) were committed by a `git add -A terraform/` on 2026-09-25.
#
# They carry no credential material — those three were `-target`ed plans and
# held no ArgoCD or GitHub resources, checked before removing them — but a plan
# embeds prior state for everything in its scope, and this repository's state is
# recorded in the SSP as holding a GitHub PAT and an OIDC client secret (P3-2).
# So the next one might. Ignored rather than remembered.
*.tfplan
*tfplan*

# Per-step Terraform logs from scripts/stack/install.sh and cleanup.sh, under
# the deployment root (tf_step in scripts/stack/targets.sh). Each holds a full
# apply or destroy, plan included, and a plan embeds prior state — the same
# reason as the plan files above. The directory also writes its own `*`
# .gitignore, for a root that lives in a deployer's repository instead.
.install-logs/

# Ignore CLI configuration files
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

*.cfg

# Written by the Packer manifest post-processor on every build. The AMI id it
# records reaches git through the PR the build workflow opens, not this file.
packer-manifest.json

.vscode/

keys/

# VPN client config contains private keys — never commit
*.ovpn
# pixi environments (root and nested, e.g. images/workbench/.pixi)
.pixi/*
!.pixi/config.toml
**/.pixi/
# pixi.lock is intentionally committed — lock files pin dependency versions
# for reproducible Docker image builds.


# vim files
.vim*
.env
.mcp.json

# Python extras
.pytest_cache
.conda

# AI Distiller
.aid

gits/

# No Serena Configs
.serena

# No Claude
.claude/*
.claude
.claude/settings.json

# Python
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Ignore temporary runtime state from Spec Kit integrations and extensions
.specify/integrations/*/state/
.specify/extensions/*/.cache/
.specify/extensions/*/tmp/

.serena/

.spec-workflow/
.superpowers/

.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# `pixi run coverage` data files (one per xdist worker before combining).
.coverage
.coverage.*
.agents

# Disposable local CSV exports from scripts/export_batch_metrics.py
metrics_exports/

# MkDocs build output (`pixi run -e docs docs-build`)
site/

# Unshareable ABCD Data
data/
backfill-qc-rejected-20260911T142606Z.jsonl
